8" class=3D"indexterm"></a><div class=3D"para">
				Rebuilding a Debian package starts with getting its source code. The ea=
siest way is to use the <code class=3D"command">apt-get source <em class=3D=
"replaceable">package-name</em></code> command. This command requires a <co=
de class=3D"literal">deb-src</code> line in the <code class=3D"filename">/e=
tc/apt/sources.list</code> file, and up-to-date index files (i.e. <code cla=
ss=3D"command">apt-get update</code>). These conditions should already be m=
et if you followed the instructions from the chapter dealing with APT confi=
guration (see <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://debian-handbook.info/browse=
/ru-RU/stable/apt.html#sect.apt-sources.list">=D0=A0=D0=B0=D0=B7=D0=B4=D0=
=B5=D0=BB&nbsp;6.1, =C2=AB=D0=A1=D0=BE=D0=B4=D0=B5=D1=80=D0=B6=D0=B8=D0=BC=
=D0=BE=D0=B5 =D1=84=D0=B0=D0=B9=D0=BB=D0=B0 <code class=3D"filename">source=
s.list</code>=C2=BB</a>). Note, however, that you will be downloading the s=
ource packages from the Debian version mentioned in the <code class=3D"lite=
ral">deb-src</code> line.
			</div><div class=3D"para">
				If you need another version, you may need to download it manually from =
a Debian mirror or from the web site. This involves fetching two or three f=
iles (with extensions <code class=3D"filename">*.dsc</code> =E2=80=94 for <=
span class=3D"emphasis"><em>Debian Source Control</em></span> =E2=80=94 <co=
de class=3D"filename">*.tar.<em class=3D"replaceable">comp</em></code>, and=
 sometimes <code class=3D"filename">*.diff.gz</code> or <code class=3D"file=
name">*.debian.tar.<em class=3D"replaceable">comp</em></code> =E2=80=94 <em=
 class=3D"replaceable">comp</em> taking one value among <code class=3D"lite=
ral">gz</code>, <code class=3D"literal">bz2</code> or <code class=3D"litera=
l">xz</code> depending on the compression tool in use), then run the <code =
class=3D"command">dpkg-source -x <em class=3D"replaceable">file.dsc</em></c=
ode> command. If the <code class=3D"filename">*.dsc</code> file is directly=
 accessible at a given URL, there is an even simpler way to fetch it all, w=
ith the <code class=3D"command">dget <em class=3D"replaceable">URL</em></co=
de> command. This command (which can be found in the <span class=3D"pkg pkg=
">devscripts</span> package) fetches the <code class=3D"filename">*.dsc</co=
de> file at the given address, then analyzes its contents, and automaticall=
y fetches the file or files referenced within. Once everything has been dow=
nloaded, it verifies the integrity of the downloaded source packages using =
<code class=3D"command">dscverify</code>, and it extracts the source packag=
e (unless the <code class=3D"literal">-d</code> or <code class=3D"literal">=
--download-only</code> option is used). The Debian keyring is needed, unles=
s the option <code class=3D"literal">-u</code> is supplied.
