 the package build process. In the simplest cases, the lines concerning the=
 initial configuration (<code class=3D"literal">./configure =E2=80=A6</code=
>) or the actual build (<code class=3D"literal">$(MAKE) =E2=80=A6</code> or=
 <code class=3D"literal">make =E2=80=A6</code> or <code class=3D"literal">c=
make =E2=80=A6</code> or =E2=80=A6) are easy to spot. If these commands are=
 not explicitly called, they are probably a side effect of another explicit=
